; setquad_sample_register: the quadratic opcodes require MODEL mode.
;
; A sample carries no quadratic storage, so SETQUAD on one has nowhere to
; write. The Rust VM resolved through `as_model_mut()` and rejected; xqvm_py
; resolved through `_get_register_as_xqmx`, which accepts a sample, and grew
; a `quadratic` map the sample's own accessors never read back -- the write
; was accepted and GETQUAD returned 0 (QUI-1160).
;
; The shared identity is TYPE_MISMATCH: `xqvm_py` names it XQMXModeError
; after the mode, the Rust VM RegisterType, and both map onto this row.
;
; The indices are in range and the value is ordinary, so nothing but the
; register's mode is at fault.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; a SAMPLE, not a model

PUSH 0           ; i
PUSH 1           ; j
PUSH 5           ; value
SETQUAD r0
HALT
